@node stereo-imager Plugin Developer Guide
@section Developer Guide

Multi-band M/S stereo width control.

@subsubheading What It Does

Controls the stereo width of audio using Mid/Side processing. The signal is split into frequency bands, and each band's stereo width can be independently adjusted — from mono (0%) through natural (100%) to hyper-wide (200%+). Useful for widening the high frequencies while keeping bass centered, or for collapsing problematic stereo information.

@subsubheading Features

@itemize @bullet
@item @strong{M/S processing}: Mid/Side encoding for precise width control
@item @strong{Multi-band}: Independent width per frequency band
@item @strong{Width range}: From mono (collapsed) to hyper-wide
@item @strong{Frequency-dependent}: Widen highs while keeping bass centered
@end itemize


